What happens internally when you run kubectl apply?
When we run kubectl apply, Kubernetes takes our YAML configuration, compares it with the existing cluster state, calculates the required changes, and sends those changes to the Kubernetes API Server.
2.The API Server processes the request, stores the desired configuration in etcd, and Kubernetes controllers work continuously to make the actual cluster state match the desired state.
The Kubernetes Controller Manager continuously watches the API Server.
The Scheduler watches for newly created Pods that do not have a node assigned.
The Kubelet running on each selected worker node detects the assigned Pod.
The Kubelet reports Pod status back to the API Server.
The Deployment Controller continues monitoring the state and ensures that the desired number of replicas is maintained.
